{
  "id": "correspondence-problem",
  "term": "correspondence problem",
  "definition": "The correspondence problem is the challenge of explaining how a person or agent can make their own body match another’s observed body movements or posture, especially when they cannot directly observe their own body from the outside. In this context, it refers to how imitation becomes possible despite limited access to both self and other body configurations.",
